(प्र- √ 5. इ) cl. 2. P. प्रैति (Ved. inf. प्रैतोस्, AitBr.), to come forth, appear, begin, RV.; BṛĀrUp.; MBh.;
to go on, proceed, advance (esp. as a sacrifice), RV.; VS.;
to go forwards or farther, come to, arrive at, enter (acc.), ib.; ŚBr.; Up.; MBh.;
to go out or away, depart (this life, with or without अस्माल् लोकात्, or इतस्), die, Br.; Up.; Mn.; MBh. &c.:
Intens. Ā. प्रेयते, to drive or go forth (said of Uṣas), RV.

(प्र-√ ईङ्ख्). P. Ā. प्रेङ्खति, ˚ते, to tremble, shake, vibrate, AitĀr.; Kāv. :
Caus. P. प्रेङ्खयति, to swing (trans.), Ragh.;
 Ā. ˚ते, to swing one's self, RV. vii, 88, 3.

(प्र-√ ईर्) Ā. प्रेर्ते, to move (intrans.), come forth, arise, appear, RV.; AV.; TS.; ŚBr. Caus. प्रेरयति, to set in motion, push on, drive forwards, urge, stimulate, excite, RV. &c. &c.;
to send, dispatch, MBh.; R.;
to turn, direct (the eyes), R.; Śak. (v.l.);
to raise (the voice), utter, pronounce (words, prayers &c.), RV.; &c.

2. प्रेष् (प्र-√ इष्) P. Ā. प्रेष्यति, ˚ते (Ved. inf. प्रेषे, Pāṇ. iii, 4, 9, Sch.; ind.p. प्रै॑षम् s.v.),
to drive on, urge, impel, send forth, RV.; MBh.;
to invite, summon, call upon (another priest to commence a recitation or a ceremony [acc.] e.g. साम प्रेष्यति, ‘he calls upon to commence the recitation of a Sāman’; esp. Impv. प्रेष्य, ‘call upon to recite or offer [acc. or gen.] to [dat.]’), ŚBr.; KātyŚr. (cf. Pāṇ. ii, 3, 61; viii, 2, 91) :
Caus. प्रेषयति, to hurl, fling, cast, throw, MBh.; R.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to turn or direct the eyes, Śak. ii, 2 (v.l. प्रेरयन्त्या);
to send forth, dismiss, dispatch, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to send into exile, banish, R.; Kathās.;
to send word, send a message to a person (gen.), R.
